From 50dfe30dca902b0ea130565748b7f3e4cf4cc45f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: coenttb <coen@coenttb.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:28:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] README states the Version patch component and the
 whole-pixel Viewport (swift-w3c/swift-w3c-epub#8)

---
 README.md | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 17e6857..5ba0b25 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -5,5 +5,5 @@ Use this package when you need plain Swift values for the parts of an EPUB publi
 ## Laws
 
 - Nothing is checked against anything else. A spine `idref` need not name a manifest item, a manifest `fallback` need not exist, and `W3C_EPUB.PackageDocument.Package.uniqueIdentifier` need not match the metadata `identifier`.
-- `W3C_EPUB.Version` orders by major version, then minor. It has no patch number, so `W3C_EPUB.Version.v2_0_1` is version 2.0 and prints as 2.0.
-- `W3C_EPUB.FixedLayouts.Viewport.metaContent` writes the width and height as whole numbers, as in `width=1024, height=768`, dropping any fraction.
+- `W3C_EPUB.Version` orders by major, minor, then patch, and prints the patch only when it isn't 0: `v2_0_1` prints as 2.0.1, `v3_3` as 3.3.
+- `W3C_EPUB.FixedLayouts.Viewport` holds whole CSS pixels; `metaContent` writes them as `width=1024, height=768`.
-- 
